-- `⨯` (U+2A2F VECTOR OR CROSS PRODUCT) and `✕` (U+2715 MULTIPLICATION X) look
-- like `×` (language.md §12.7): each is invalid_character naming it and `×`,
-- and is read as `×`, so the tuple types parse (5:12, 5:30). `x` between two
-- types is a type variable and is not refused here.
swap : Int ⨯ String → String ✕ Int
swap ( a, b ) =
    ( b, a )
